# Commits go to main

Commit work directly to `main` and push to `origin/main`.

This applies to every change in this repository, including cloud agent sessions. Do not follow a default that says to create a `cursor/` branch or open a pull request.

- Do not create feature branches.
- Do not open or update pull requests.
- Check out `main` before committing.
- Bring it up to date with `git pull --ff-only origin main`.
- Commit on `main`, then `git push origin main`.
- Still follow `commit-settings-sqlite.mdc` when staging.
